# eas-cli reads this file (next to app.json/eas.json).
# Without it, when the working tree has uncommitted changes, eas-cli switches
# to a tar-of-the-working-tree mode that can include locally-present
# gitignored content. That's how a local Windows-pathed
# apps/mobile/android/build/generated/autolinking/autolinking.json once
# leaked onto the EAS Linux builder and made every autolinked RN library
# resolve to a `/home/expo/.../apps/mobile/android/C:/Users/njoub/...` path,
# yielding "No matching variant of project ... No variants exist" for all
# of them.

# Native projects are regenerated by `expo prebuild` on EAS; never upload
# the local copy.
android/
ios/build/

# Gradle caches can also carry absolute, host-specific paths.
.gradle/
